GitOps Interview Questions & Revision

✨ Hello DevOps Learners!
Continuing my GitOps learning journey after completing Ansible, today I’m doing a complete revision of GitOps concepts along with important interview questions 🚀
This is the final step to prepare for real DevOps interviews confidently.

🔹 Important Interview Concepts
 Make sure you are clear with:
GitOps principles (Declarative, Version Control, Reconciliation)
Git as Single Source of Truth
Push vs Pull model
ArgoCD workflow and architecture
Auto Sync & Self-Healing
Multi-environment deployments

🔹 Scenario-Based Questions
 Interviewers often ask real-world scenarios like:
What will you do if production goes down after deployment?
How will you handle configuration drift?
Staging works but production fails — why?
How do you roll back a failed deployment?
These test your practical understanding, not just theory.

🔹 Quick Revision Strategy
Revise all GitOps workflows
Practice explaining architecture clearly
Focus on real-world use cases
Understand tool integration (CI/CD + GitOps)

💡 Key Insight:
 Strong GitOps knowledge combined with real-world scenarios and clear explanations is the key to cracking DevOps interviews.
